\section{Discussion}
The splitting type's information about the residue class is capped by the abelianization, and the unexplained part of the type is capped by $\lb|G'|$. The ceiling $\lb[G:G']$ is attained exactly for complete readouts, and perfect groups leak nothing. The law does not by itself predict synergy of batteries; that is the sign of $I(c;T_2\mid T_1)-I(c;T_2)$. Faithfulness of the type encoding is a genuine experimental hazard in degree six.

\section{Open problems}
\begin{conjecture}[Sandwich equality]
$I=H(T)-\lb|G'|$ iff $T$ is injective on every coset of $G'$. For the cycle-type readout this holds only for abelian groups.
\end{conjecture}
\begin{conjecture}[Dihedral ladder]
For $x^{2m}-2$ (group $D_{2m}$) the faithful channel has a closed form in $m$, the loss is strictly positive for $m\ge3$, and the loss of the quartic record tends to a limit.
\end{conjecture}
\begin{conjecture}[Conditional battery capacity]
For class-function dials, $I(c;T_2\mid T_1)\le\lb[G:G']-I(c;T_1)$, with equality iff $(T_1,T_2)$ jointly determine the coset. Positive synergy is governed by the double-coset structure of the conjugacy classes.
\end{conjecture}
Further targets: a rigorous converse for the ``barrier-4'' phenomenon, production-scale subexponential experiments ($N\ge2^{64}$), conductor identification for $D_5$ fields, and degree-six groups beyond $D_6$ and regular $S_3$.

\appendix
\section{The arithmetic dictionary}
Let $K$ be the splitting field of $f$ and $G=\mathrm{Gal}(K/\mathbb{Q})$. For an unramified prime $p$, the orbits of $\Frob_p$ on the roots correspond to the irreducible factors of $f\bmod p$, with orbit lengths equal to degrees. By Chebotarev, the density of primes with Frobenius class $C$ is $|C|/|G|$. By Kronecker--Weber, $K^{G'}\subseteq\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_m)$, and the restriction of $\Frob_p$ to $K^{G'}$ is the image of $p\bmod m$ in $G/G'$. Hence (residue of $p$, splitting type) is asymptotically distributed as $(gG',\text{cycle type of }g)$ with $g$ uniform on $G$.

